        "original_id": "313d66e7-d9b4-5f8a-bf5c-6ca9df4d51b4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pravda, Stiffelio, Aroldo\n- People: Giuseppe Verdi, Francesco Maria Piave, Lajos Magyar\n- Organizations: Communist Party of the Soviet Union, Comintern\n- Topics: opera, newspapers\n\nFacts:\n- In 1850, Giuseppe Verdi and Francesco Maria Piave collaborated on the opera Stiffelio, which has three acts and an Italian libretto by Piave.\n- Aroldo is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto by Francesco Maria Piave, and it was based on and adapted from their earlier collaboration Stiffelio.\n- In 1922, Lajos Magyar went to the Soviet Union in a prisoner exchange and worked on the staff of the Comintern and at the newspaper Pravda.\n- Pravda is a Russian broadsheet newspaper whose name means \"Truth.\"\n- Pravda was formerly the official newspaper of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union.\n- Pravda was once one of the most influential newspapers in the Soviet Union and had a circulation of 11 million.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
